Today the last of our 5 DECagent90 died after only about 2 and a half year.
Rest In Peace. There were not in the same building or on the same LAN.

We had also to replace umpteen dead DECbridge90 (died with a burned out
transformator coil "It smells like AMPERE"). Someone told me, that is is
a "known bug".

All this happened over the last about 8 months. We did not have such problems
before. At least, not that I know of.

Digital had some kind of a "replacement price" of about 50% percent of a new
one. But that is long (?) gone now. Currently we do not want to buy such
a short living thing again. And of course not for the "full" price.

Do you have such bad experiences with DEChub90 equipment, too ?

-Peter

PS: Last week we got the second PORTswitch 900TP (of about 20) which was DOA...
And last month my boss got a little electrical shock of a DEChub900 (some
backpanel pins - not the 220V ones - of the Power Supplies were bent again).
Currently its getting harder for me: I suggested the DEChub and still like it.
