We can safely assume that we'll lose one of our 50 or so DECBridge
90's every other thunderstorm. They fry with that familiar smell.

We also have a fair number of problems with DECRepeater 90's, not with
single ports going out but generally the whole unit.

Many of our hubs are in telephone closets, we have had self-made problems with
cross connect wire from the telephone 66 blocks falling in the power supplies
and shorting them or causing the fan to stop and burning them out.

We have had no signfigicant problems with our DECHub 900 except for a 
gotcha with placement of 32 port repeaters which was noted somewhere in
the readme for the device.

