In article <867543878snz@p850ug1.demon.co.uk>,
Tony Duell <ard@p850ug1.demon.co.uk> wrote:

>I can't remember if the 11/44 fans have ball races or not. If they do, damage
>to the shaft is a lot less likely.

The fan that I repaired had these -- however, the three fans were not
all from the same manufacturer, so, the others may or may not have had
these ball races in them.

>I use 'high melting point grease' (Castrol LM - I'm not sure what the US
>equivalent is). It's a sort of general-purpose grease that you'd use on
>cars if no other grease was specified.

Just make sure that it's a high melting point grease; I didn't find
the Castrol LM, but I did find No. 2 General Purpose and Wheel Bearing
Grease made by Quaker State.  (don't forget to soak the ball races,
etc. in white spirits or turpentine overnight to remove all of the old
grease before repacking the bearings)

If ball races aren't used, I seem to recall (correctly?) that a
lighter weight oil, not grease, is to be used.

