In article <5p04t2$od3$1@nuke.csu.net>, jkatz@ultrix6.cs.csubak.edu (jeremy)
writes:
:1- can someone please point me to some info (capacity and jumper
:configurations) on RZ drives, in particular the RZ23 and 24.

   The RZ23 series is 104 MB.  The RZ24 series is 209 MB.

   The jumper settings are specific to individual members of the RZ23 and
   RZ24 series -- please confirm that these drives do not have an additional
   letter, such as "RZ24E", associated with the drive model name.

:2- I need to build a cable to use a vga moitor in a VAXstation, so i need
:a map of the pins/purpose for a vax monitor.

   Which VAXstation?  [Not that it matters in this case, as I know of no
   VGA-compatible VAXstation controller for any of the various VAXstation
   series systems sold.]

   In other words, this signal conversion likely requires rather more than
   a cable, as the QVSS and QDSS series VAXstation graphics controllers
   (Q-bus), and the derivative GPX and SPX controllers found on VAXstation
   (non-Q-bus) 3100 series systems, are not compatible with VGA.

   There are a number of folks with VR-series VAXstation monitors they
   cannot use with VGA or SVGA graphics controllers, so you may/will want
   to acquire one of these.  VR160, VR260, VR290, VR292, VR297, and VR299
   series monitors should work on most VAXstation systems.

