I had a vendor try to pull that one on me.  I refused to accept it.
I simply asked what the pricing structure was for the *same*
product on NT, and then demanded that they justify charging me more
for it on UNIX.  The only argument they presented that I agreed
with was that, for the product in question, they sold far more on
Win* than they did on UNIX.  I gave 'em a margin for that and we
agreed on an acceptable price.

The alternative that I presented to them was this: since I wasn't
going to pay the outrageous asking price for a UNIX version, my only
other option was to go Win* for my solution.  At which point there
was no longer any need to stick with *their* product alone--being as
there were lots of competing products in the Win*-only environment.
*That* really got their attention :-).

