In article <33B27BFD.38EF@bbc.co.uk>, Tim Llewellyn <tim.llewellyn@bbc.co.uk> writes:

> So, out of interest, if one has a VMS listings CD, is one allowed
> to mount it on a machine with a network connection.

There is a restriction that the listing CD's are to be used on a
single machine.  That does not prohibit a network connection,
but they don't want you buying one copy of the listings and having
too many people use them.  I would feel it was fair to mount them
on one machine but always use them from another, but they would
really like to be able to sell more than one copy to really large
customers.

Like many licensing questions, it is hard to legislate "fairness",
so one ends up with things a bit fuzzy around the edges.

