X-Deja-AN: 252865048
Distribution: world
References: <33B1A55E.786A@ps.net>
Organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
Reply-To: alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com (Alan Rollow - Dr. File System's Home for Wayward Inodes.)
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec



The point of the V3.0 release of Digital UNIX was to add MP
support.  I think the network drivers, the tty driver, the
SCSI driver, UFS, most of the core kernel stuff were all made
MP friendly.  Notice what got left out?  AdvFS.  It wasn't
made MP friendly until V4.0.  If you're using AdvFS for your
busy file systems this could be the source of the problem.

Interrupts are handled by the boot processor, but quickly handed
off to distribute the real load.  I suspect the only other
subsystem not made MP friendly was the MSCP stack, but that's
just a guess.
--
