This is not correct, at least not unless you also have some sort of third
party PDF filter installed on your system.  "Out of the box" the CDAviewer
will do postscript, but not PDF, at least on OpenVMS.

>> Also XPDF is available freely from the known archives for both platforms.
>Only if you want to spend time putting the LZW decompressor back
>in that the author left out to avoid incurring the wrath of
>Univac.

XPDF runs on OpenVMS and Unix, as stated. While the author did take out
LZW, he added a work around, a callout to gzip, look in config.h and you'll
find: 

#define uncompressCmd "gzip -d -q"

Just make sure you have the right defines in your make/build procedure.

