Geert Haustraete wrote:
> 
> I want to install a DEC Etherworks 3 Turbo networkcard in my config running
> NT 4.0 WS.
> I have the following hardware:

[snip]
 
> Who has experience in installing a DEC205 and can give me some clues?
> Help is appreciated.

For one: The driver for the EtherWORKS 3 (EWRK3) series of boards
(a.k.a. DE203, DE204, DE205) does *NOT* come on the Windows NT kit.

In other words, you need to get the drivers separately.

Secondly: Try ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/adapters for the latest
EWRK3 drivers.

Note also that the first batch of EtherWORKS 3 boards (some years
ago) has a problem where the card grabs all IRQ's it can be configured
for (regardless of the config settings).

First workaround: Cut the etch for the leads for unused IRQs
(permanently
configuring the board ;-) or cover the leads with non-conducting tape.

Solution: Ask Digital to swap for a working board (there was an 
intermediate release with jumpers to select the IRQ).

Other than that I've had no problems with EtherWORKS 3 boards.

