>Not me.  But you bring back memories.  I was the I/O interface 
>designer/supporter at the former Lexidata for all kinds of machines (can 
>you say Perkin-Elmer :)), but I never stashed away any spare boards in 
>my trunk :).  Too bad you can't use the Unibus interface that you 
>currently have in the VAX on another machine that supports the Unibus.

Could something like a QUNIVERTER work?  I've moved plenty of UNIBUS
devices to MicroVAXs using bus converter boards from MDB systems, and
MOST of them can be operated transparently:

DEC DR11-W
DEC DMF-32 (and 3rd party equivalents)
DEC UDA-50 (" " ")
MDA FIRE recorder
RAMTEK 9400 series displays
FPS 5000 series array processors
APTEC IOC-24

Some of the 3rd party interfaces required minor modifications to the
device drivers to get them to look at the right address space.  But for
the most part, they worked just fine through the Qbus/Unibus converter.
Of course, this was many years ago, and I don't rememebr how it was
done, even though I did most of them.

