Oh boy!

Many high-energy physics experiments digitze raw data in the 10's of 
GB/sec range.

The limits in current technology (mainly data handling & storage) force us 
to try really hard to pick the good from the bad recorded events on the fly,
with the danger that we throw away interesting information.

Just assume another leap in storage technology and then calculate for yourself,
