Subject: Alpha NTFS Partition
Date: 1997/06/25
Message-ID: <33b140b7.155331945@news.stortek.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 252500601
Organization: Storage Technology Corporation
Reply-To: Kurt_Schumacher@stortek.com
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I thought I would update everyone who responded to my query on how to
create an NTFS partition on my Alpha system. 

I would have responded to the individuals who emailed me, but we were just
converted to Microsoft Exchange and the internet addresses in my folders
got lost in the conversion. (Please, don't spawn any threads about Exchange
here!) Anyway, this might be of general interest.

What I found out from DEC is that the version of AlphaBIOS for the K2 chip
on my system does not include a critical function that allows me to change
a partition from system to non-system so that it can be converted to NTFS.
An upcoming BIOS version is supposed to contain this function.

In the meantime, we have found a workaround:

1) Install NT on a FAT partition
2) Bring up NT and use the Disk Manager to define a new partiton, and
format it as NTFS
3) Install NT on the new NTFS partition
4) Bring up the new NT system and use the Disk Manager to delete the FAT
partition, define a new partition, and format it as NTFS

It's ugly, but it works.

Thanks for everyone who responded to my initial message.

Kurt G. Schumacher
Storage Technology Corporation



