I'm curious about the C/C++ options available for alpha under
WinNT.  We submitted some benchmarks to DEC for compilation
under both WinNT (VC++) and DEC Unix, and the Unix performance
was apparently quite a bit higher (the DEC rep ran the
benchmark under NT, but complained about the outcome and only
returned Unix results).  This situation surprised me,
since both compilers use the GEM core.  According to one DEC
rep, the VC++ front end did not supply enough info to the
core for aggressive optimizations; ostensibly, this shortcoming
will be remedied "soon".

As a result, the alpha WinNT benefit over the WinNT PPro was
perhaps not as great as one might expect.



