I would agree that current growth may not be due to availability
of kernel source per se, but it simply *is* the reason it grew 
to something worthwhile for all the folks using it now.  That
is un-deniable.  This enthusiasm trickles down from the core
developers to the end users who jump on the bandwagon now.  It's
a domino effect for sure...

>>Doesn't it also contribute to the emergence
>>of a large number of developers who otherwise never would have gotten into
