>
>However, Linux was hardly the first OS out there that ran on PCs
>and had full source available. Minix preceeded it by several years,
>and that never had anywhere near the same amount of popularity.

Correct me if I'm wrong, but Minix isn't and never was under
a truly "free" license...it is free for ed use, but it is not for
commercial use.  Linus also chose to write his own kernel because
of deficiencies he saw in Minix.  Others chose to help with 
development for the same reason...they either couldn't use Minix
for free or they didn't like it (and avoided *BSD due to those
nasty court battles occuring, I believe).

That is my understanding...I wasn't really involved in this
stuff at that point, so I welcome corrections.


