In article <33a9c5f3.2634093@netnews.worldnet.att.net>, mhking@worldnet.att.net (Michael King) writes:
> I recently acquired a DEC GIGI and a VR295-DA monitor.  I need a few
> items of information about these two pieces of equipment.  Firstly, do
> they work/would they work together?  Does the GIGI normally turn on
> and have all lights on except Local?  What are its rear switch
> settings?  Thanks in advance.

Although they both use Sync on Green RGB, I don't know if that monitor
will work with it (I'd have to drag my GIGI to work to find out).  Do
you have a cheap mono monitor with a composite video input?  If so,
try plugging that into the mono connector on the back (an RCA to BNC
converter plug or cable will probably be required).

After the fifteen second power-on self-test, the only light on should be
the on-line light.  The light pattern you mention is not one of the
valid self-test failure codes.  Try setting all the rear switches to
the down position.

Until you get it to pass self-test, there is little use in trying to attach
a monitor.


George
