Mind you, there's at least one price comparison that hurts Unix, and
makes management get uppity: SQL Server for NT is a damn sight cheaper
than an Oracle license.  We're going to run our next manufacturing
database on Oracle, Solaris and Sun, but the Oracle license is a lot of
money.  A _lot_ of money.  There's also the fact that a lot of vendors
sell essentially the same product for Unix and NT/Win95, expect the MS
version is (a) better and (b) about a tenth of the price.  Framemaker
leaps to mind.

