> NT and determined that it would cost up to (a minimum of?) 2x
> what it's costing them to do what they do with UNIX right now.

I think that to extrapolate from ISP to ``Enterprise'' is a slight leap
of faith.  I don't think too many people would seriously dispute that if
you want to do ISP-type things Unix is a good home: the software base is
there, and the staff are there.  How many people with deep mail, Web,
