Since the late 80s, the VMS source listings have been available on CD.
Simple to grep, search, or (with the free cvtlis tool) compile.

Microfiche was used earlier, but you must recall that from the mid
70s to late 80s, fiche readers could be found and CDs were either
rare or did not exist at all.

I don't recall seeing sources to Solaris kicking around in any such
form when we had a few thou of them at GE to admin...

Colleges got a special deal for unix sources at some times in the
past, as those who are slightly dry behind the ears will recall,
but commercially these deals were not even close. Back in the
70s I believe the commercial fee for unix source was 40 or 50 K
(which was worth more then thanks to some real serious inflation
back then...remember the ~15%/year inflation we had for a while...?)




