>The specint95 is higher also.  By the time Sun gets to 500 Mhz, I'm sure
>Digital will be selling faster MUCH machines... i.e. 21264 based systems
>over twice as fast as todays.

The clock rate for a single CPU is only one factor in a large
equation.  Even just looking at MIPS you have to consider the ability
of the kernel to do MP threads efficiently, the bus and backplane
speeds, and of course cost.

The maximum number of CPUs would seem to be at least as important as
clock rates.  Sparc supports 64 CPUs (in the 10K) but I haven't seen an
Alpha that supports more than 14 (or is it 12, in the 8400).  That
would seem to be a substantial difference (300*64=19,200,
500*14=6,000).

Roger Marquis



