Network logins, or serial port logins? Assuming they're network logins,
get 25 old 386 boxes with 8-16MB of memory, install a 16-bit Ethernet
card in each one, install Linux, and run 16 concurrent processes on each
one logging into your cluster, copying a file or something, then logging
out, ad infinitum.

