Hello,
	In the dim dark past, DEC once sold an option called the LS11, which 
was a Centronics printer attached to an LP11 unibus card via a cable with 
berg-to-Amphenol connections.

 Several years ago(1983-1994), I found the printset ( schematics) for this
cable and made a short version fron a ribbon cable and an IDC Amphenol
connector. I attached this to an LAV11(predecessor to the LPV11) card in a
Qbus system running under RT11 and XXDP+ and appeared to work with my
Sekochia? (GP100) printer (but had problems with my TOYO printer/plotter). 

There is also a newer parallel printer interface the LPV11-Sa (m8186?)which
has two printer ports on the on card with D25 connectors on the handle .
If you need it I might be able to find a list of pin/signal-names in my 
old notes(unless one of the DECies can find my old entry in one of the NOTES 
conferences any quicker).

Regards,
	Peter (formerly GIDDAY:: or RIPPER::)BARLIN



