In article <33A89A26.412C@ix.netcom.com>, Jim Reid <jcreid@ix.netcom.com> writes:
:...noticed on the back panel of the [MicroVAX II] system there is a 9
:pin D-style connector which I assume can be used as a console port.

  One uses an H8571-B DECconnect adapter to get to DECconnect MMJ -- this
  adapter will likely be easily available.

  On most VAXstation and MicroVAX systems:

	1 - pgnd - protective ground
        2 - txd - transmit data
        3 - rxd - receive data
        4 - rts - request to send
        5 - dtr - data terminal ready
        6 - dsr - data set ready
        7 - sgnd - signal ground
        8 - "option present" - shorted to 9
        9 - "option present" - shorted to 8

  The VAXstation and MicroVAX 2000 needed a short between pins 8 and 9,
  to indicate the presence of an option.  Most (all?) other systems left
  both pins 8 and 9 "floating" (disconnected).

  [I've passed this pinout along for inclusion into the OpenVMS FAQ; the
  MMJ pinout and DECconnect adapter information is already in the FAQ.]

