In article <33A85FB7.5C08@skilling.com>, Kevin Westfall <krw@skilling.com> writes:
:...Our consultant said that we must be setup for
:Xon/Xoff because the VAX does not support hardware handshaking.  The
:people at Ganson Engineering seemed to think that info was incorrect.

  Many DIGITAL serial line controllers support only XON/XOFF flow control
  and most software typically expects no flow control, or (more commonly)
  XON/XOFF flow control.  RTS/CTS (hardware) flow control isn't nearly as
  common on DIGITAL systems.

  Check the terminal controller to see if it even supports RTS/CTS.

  Most folks working with this configuration use a LAT terminal server
  (LATprint or DECserver).

  And the DIGITAL DCPS-Open package is the package generally used with
  third-party Postscript printers.  (I'm not specifically familiar with
  the HP 5siMX, nor do I know if DCPS supports it.  On average, HP seems
  to release three new printers a year.  Or more.)

