In article <EBrs11.IzB@world.std.com>, allison@see.sig (Allison) writes:
:hoffman@xdelta.enet.dec.nospam (Stephen Hoff Hoffman) wrote:
:
:>   The DEQNA Ethernet controllers are not supported on recent OpenVMS
:>   versions, use a DELQA or DESQA (the latter only for a BA2xx or BA4xx
:>   series enclosure)...
:Actually at least through version 5.4-4 I can state that the DEQNA is
:supported (meaning the driver is there and runs).

  Longtime readers of the group would know I would not generally refer
  to V5.4-3 as "recent" :-), given the current OpenVMS release is V7.1.

  DEQNA support was officially dropped in V5.0.

  The DELQA and DESQA are preferable for various reasons, including
  system and network performance.

  Both VMScluster and LAT protocols ceased allowing use of the DEQNA
  starting in the V5.5 release -- the last release one could use a
  DEQNA for these protocols was V5.4-3.  (DECnet-Plus also has no
  DEQNA support.)

  The DEQNA driver was still present in V5.5 for use by application
  protocols.

  Given used/refurb prices, I'd acquire a DELQA (BA23/BA123/BA200/BA400,
  depending on the cabinet kit) or DESQA (BA200/BA400 only), and commit
  the DEQNA to the museum for first-generation Ethernet controllers.

