Kevin Westfall wrote:
> installed a new HP 5siMX printer equiped with a Ganson Engineering
> XPort serial interface card to communicate with the VAX.  We are now
> having intermittant print problems. 

I have a MicrovaxII with DHQ11 serial boards. These support modem
controls. However, VMS doesn't officially support hardware handshaking
at 5.5-2.

But: There is the /COMMSYNC qualifier in SET TERMINAL which was designed
for printers. It does take advantage of hardware flow control for
printers (but not for modems for supposedly security reasons).

So, hardware handshaking works with /COMMSYNC .

Furthermore, with the /MODEM qualifier, I have found that the DHQ11 does
seem to support hardware flow control even if VMS doesn't know about it.

Make sure your cable between the vax and printer is a full modem cable
(pins 2,3,4,5,6,7,8,20) and that your printer is set accordingly.



