>Kessack Young-Smith  <kessack.young-smith@bt-sys.bt.co.uk> wrote:
>>**QBUS(LSI11) vs UNIBUS**
>>Can anyone give me a succinct description of ESSENTIAL differences.

The biggest difference is the Q-bus is time multiplexed address and
data where the unibus is seperate data and address lines.  There are
an assortment of control lines on unibus that qbus didn't need or were
accomplished in other ways.  Q-bus was a designed effort to lower the
cost and simplify the backplane for lower cost LSI-11 cpus.

