My information is based on the pcXL server which, I believe, is the
same.  I believe the difference is in the daughtercard. If my
assumptions are correct:
This machine is basically the same as the prioris xl.  The mother board
is a 54-23456-01 which si the same one in the original Prioris. 
(According to what I have been told by DEC.)  The SCSI interface is an
adaptec 7870.  This is documented onscreen during bootup and on the
chip.  This interface is the same as the adaptec 2940 (according to
adaptec).  There is a jumper 'j22' on the MLB that must be 'on' in order
to enable wide scsi.  This interface does not support ultrawide scsi. 
Whether you can use both interfaces simultaneously I haven't been able
to determine.  You may have to adapt a narrow cable to the wide cable. 
Suggest reading up on the subject at adaptec.com.  Let me know if this
helps.



