Chuck McCrobie wrote:
> 
> I currently have a BA123 cabinet with the KA630 CPU (16 MB of RAM).
> This is a QBUS machine (obviously).  I'm interested in upgrading the
> machine to a faster CPU (and corresponding memory).  I know I can get
> the KA655 CPU and memory in the BA123 cabinet, but this offers a VUP
> rating of 3.8.  While this is ~3x faster than the KA630 I have now (0.9
> VUP), I would like to "jazz" the machine up even more.
> 
> The FAQ I have lists the VAX 4000 series as being QBUS machines.  Is it
> possible to put those CPUs in the BA123 cabinet?
> 
>   KA660 (VAX 4000 M200)

  No, requires BA213/BA215 enclosure. This is due to the H3602 Console
  module the KA660 needs, the CPU board itself fits in the cabinet.
  AFAIK there is no KA660 console module for the BA123. 

>  KA690 (VAX 4000 M400)
>  KA69D (VAX 4000 M50x)
>  KA700 (VAX 4000 M600/M700)

  No, require BA440 enclosure

>  KA1303? (VAX 4000 M10x)

  They are in a self-contained enclosure. When Q-bus expansion is
needed, 
  the BA123 can be connected through Q-bus expansion cabling.
  
