In article <EBMBJC.C9J.0.bloor@torfree.net>, cr389@torfree.net (Yin Tse) writes:
> I'm trying to change the font size of a queue and I've tried to 
> change the form of the queue, but the font size didn't change 
> although the form did change. What was wrong in there , did I 
> forget to change something else ? Thanks for the help.
> 
Hello,

without knowing the type of queue and the type of printer, I'm just going to
pass off some ideas.

You are most likely going to need the escape sequences for the desired
font sizes.  You would place them into a text file, such as

landscape.txt
<ESC>E<ESC>&l1O<ESC>(8U<ESC>(sp16.66h8.5vs-1b0T<ESC>&l8D

you would create and place landscape.txt into a device control library:

lib/crea dave landscape.txt/text, or if queue already has a device control
library, then
librar/inser LIBname.tlb landscape.txt

GVAX08> lib/lis dave.tlb
Directory of TEXT library USR$TOXICOL:[COCHRAN]DAVE.TLB;1 on 17-JUN-1997
08:54:0
1
Creation date:  17-JUN-1997 08:53:55      Creator:  VAX-11 Librarian V04-00
Revision date:  17-JUN-1997 08:53:55      Library format:   3.0
Number of modules:      1                 Max. key length:  39
Other entries:          0                 Preallocated index blocks:     11
Recoverable deleted blocks:      0        Total index blocks used:        1
Max. Number history records:      20      Library history records:        0

LANDSCAPE
GVAX08> 
copy dave.tlb to sys$common:[syslib]

init/queue dave/librar=dave  (plus whatever else you have)


Now, (we're almost done)

modify your form and add /setup=landscape. Now whenever you print with form, 
the setup module will place the escape sequences from the device control
library ahead of your print job. simply replace the sequence shown in the
example above with the escape sequences for the desired font.

dave cochran



