Both poster are probably right: part of this comes from a common confusion:
many people use
68K or MC68K as a shorthand for 68000, 68010, 68020, 68030, 68040, etc...
which is a sueful shorthand, but causes in exactly this case, i.e.,
in doing analysis of the ISA, 68000/68010 are actually quite different
