	this case plays a TREMENDOUS role.  To quote Dr. Glenn Everhart
	(following can be found on http://www.dejanews.com/ searching
	for:  Glenn and galaxies and decus)

	------

	"Galaxies is a VMS technology. Not NT, not unix, not anything else.
	You get VMS and when VMS supports Galaxies ("should be soon":)
	you get the 10x performance with suitable hardware. Some of the
	suitable hardware exists now, and the 10x performance presumes
	a large configuration.

	The factor 10 comes about because VMS can scale its performance
	with this technology better than anything else. Thus if all you
	have is a few CPUs, the advantage will be less. However, even a
	handful of processors will have some advantages."

