	I/O load the better.  Galaxies scales compared to other OS's.  Glenn
	made mention Galaxy will do as well as or better.   Where the
	processing does no communication and very little I/O (CPU bound)
	Galaxies does as well.  Obviously, large RDBMS is a huge I/O hog
	and hence the 10x number is bandied about.

	Informix is reportedly porting back to VMS.  You don't undertake
	a big effort such as that on a whim.  

