In article <1997Jun13.154254.1@eisner>, 
brooks_r@eisner.decus.org (Rob Brooks) writes:
|>> Isn't there a SCSI QBUS card for general disk access - I haven't ever seen 
|>> one, but I just thought there might be one... or I guess I have to use another 
|>> one of my CMD CQD223/M controllers...
|>	Try the KFQSA (M7769)  Which cabinet are you using?
|>
|>

The KFQSA is a Q-bus DSSI interface, not a SCSI interface. You could hang one
of the HSD devices off the DSSI and then hang SCSI drives off that.

The KZQSA (M5976) is a Q-bus SCSI interface, but is not supported for
magnetic disks (only for tapes, CDROMs and optical devices).

The RZQX1 (M5977) is a Q-bus SCSI interface used on the latest PDP-11s. It
does support the use of magnetic disks but is not supported on VAXes (or
by OpenVMS).

Antonio

