> I am using run/detached to schedule a daily job at a particular fixed
> time and it works fine. However, I have a question on that. When I do
> a
>         $show user "myusername"  /full
> it does not show this job. The process was initiated from my account
> and in fact doing a
>         $show process /continuous /id=xxxxxxxxxxxx
> indicates that the process has the same uid as my account.
> 
> So why does this process not show up on a "show user". Batch jobs do.

A 'user' process is every interactive, batch or network process.
Detached processes, even with a CLI environment created by LOGINOUT, are
not considered as 'user' process and therefore not displayed by SHOW
USER.

