James Smith <js42@infinet.com> wrote:
>I only want the micro proccesor, but I'll deal with the whole thing.
>I'm only looking for the 233mhz Alpha.  E-mail with what you have at
>js42@infinet.com  Thanks everybody!

If you want a 233MHz Alpha microprocessor in a useful state, a dead Multia
will likely do you little or no good.

At least on my Multia, the processor is not socketed -- it's soldered on to
the motherboard.  Also, you should be aware that the Multia doesn't use a
21064 microprocessor like the "real" DEC workstations of that vintage; it uses
a 21066, which is a cut-down version of the 21064 with a slower bus. 

