Hi.

I hope that someone can help me with this: I have a configuration
with an AlphaServer running Digital UNIX v4.0a, a DECserver 90TL
and a Digital LA30W printer on a serial line via this 90TL (LAT).

If I try to print some preformatted document to the LA30W, either
by using 'lpr -x -Pla30w file.name' or by using the more low-level
substitute 'cat file.name >> /dev/tty08' (tty08 being a LAT device),
the printer receives numerous BELL signs. These BELLs appear random-
ly within the data (a hexdump on the printer shows that), but don't
affect the data itself. The printing speed reduces greatly, because
of all these BELLs sounding all the time... Speed reduction by a
factor of 8 is not rare at all.

So printing slows down if a BELL character is introduced in normal
text, but if it is inserted within an escape code sequence, strange
things happen. This means that long documents always break somewhere
along the line.

