DIA0: is the RF30, a smallish DSSI drive and probably your best bet on
booting this unless you have a boot tape. Since you entered ESA0 in
the above boot, the default is probably set to that right now. Try to
boot from the disk as follows:
	>>> BOOT DIA0
If this works, set the default boot by:
	>>> SET BOOT DIA0
If the boot fails, there is probably not an operating system on the
disk. If you can get an OS tape, you could install a system to the
disk from it. I know you can get a VMS v6.1 CD from DECUS for $30.00.
I don't know if they are offering othre media or not.

ESA0: is the ethernet adapter. You probably won't be able to boot with
this unless you have other vaxen around to boot from. Not likely since
you are new to vax ;7)

Good luck,
Steve



