Saeid Zoonematkermani wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> A few days ago I tried to install SP3 on a Multia running NT4 and some how
> one important system file (shell32.dll) got corrupted during the
> installation and the machine would not boot afterwards. Emergency Recovery
> Disk could not fix the problem and I eventaully resorted to reinstalling
> NT from CD-ROM. I also had to reinstall FX!32 but it cannot see the old
> database containing all the optimized code any more. My question is
> whether there is any way to convince FX!32 to use the old database for the
> optimized code. I made a backup of that folder on a separate disk but
> unfortunately that is the only thing backed up.
> 
> Any help would be appreciated. Thanks in advance,
> 
> - Saeid

To me it sounds like, if you installed the Intel version of SP3.

Whenever you do NT-system installations, that might cause a
reinstallation
of FX!32, always make an export of profiles from within FX!32, that way
you will always be able to import your profiles again.

What might be missing though, is the sys32x86 directory(located inside
the
WINNT directory), since you did a complete NT reinstallation. This
directory
contains all the win32 x86 related stuff, used by your x86 programs.

Anyhow, if you still have that directory, you should be able to setup an
additional database search path from FX!32 Manager under:

		Options
			Preferences-
				     Advanced.

Hope this helps

	Anders Blicher Petersen



