Huh?  Sorry, any system which dies when anyone sends three characters to
one of several TCP ports is not a real operating system...

And I ran a system which had one Netware server running as the Groupwise
server for an organisation, which provided internal mail for 350 staff,
a fax gateway, MIME/UUencoded/BINHEX support on an SMTP gateway,
asynchronous dial-in access to mail, and Web access to mail, all while
acting as a normal file and print server with over 1Gb of application
