Yeah, its like finding an oasis in the desert.....and then realising
that one of the previous sheep died in the water.  The management
features of NT are OK, but they're not unique, and they don't scale at
all well - compare NT domains with NDS and you immediately see
limitations in NT.  Compare NT disk support with Unix, and you
immediately see limitations in NT.  Compare NT maturity with anything
else, and you'll roll about laughing - at this stage, having gaping
security and reliability holes in the basic OS which have yet to be
patched (and with no sign of any action from Microsoft) is criminal.

