And don't forget that all those Enterprise features being added such
as fault tolerance, better SMP scaleability, and clustering.

Oh and Microsoft is also trying to make NT the best Java environment
and whatever else they can dominate....

The biggest problem I see is that currently 99% of all NT licenses run
on Intel, and while Intel CPU's are impressive, they are way behind in
multiple CPU configurations and reliablility.

And don't get me started on the fact that NT is only as reliable as it
worst written device driver, which on Intel can be one of thousands
of commodity PCI/ISA hardware.

I like NT, but Microsoft tends to bite off more than it can chew.

