In article <01bc7784$8a7a71c0$03cc1dcc@dgardner.fnxgrp.com>, "Dan Gardner" <dan.gardner@c2technologies.com> writes:
:I'm trying to set up a DEQFA on a VAX 4000 - 106a
:
:I'm trying to configure UCX (version 3.3) on an VMS 6.1 system.  When you
:startup UCX it hangs up on the DEQFA device and finally times out.

   I'd upgrade to UCX V4.1, with the current ECO.

   It would appear -- based on little information -- that there is
   an interrupt vector and/or CSR set wrong somewhere in the Q-bus.
   (It looks like at least one interrupt vector is wrong, but these
   sorts of problems can cascade among multiple modules...)

   (I have not checked to see if UCX V3.3 has support for a DEQFA.)

   One must run a SYSGEN> CONFIGURE, specifying *every* Q-bus board
   present in the system, save the list of requested CSR and vector
   settings, shut down, and then pull each module out of the Q-bus
   and verify the CSR and interrupt vector are set to expected values.

  -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
