Doesn't sound like the same problem but . . .
I put a Conner 1060S in my Celebris XL (NCR810 SCSI on the mainboard) and
couldn't get it to configure without
a. putting the original Quantum Fireball at a SCSI ID lower than the
Quantum.
b. low level formatting the Conner before using disk administrator on it
(NT fdisk).

FYI the 1060S ships with write caching disabled, probably same on the W. I
used Adaptec's EZ-SCSI to enable it. A Win NT Raid 0 stripe set of the two
drives gets me real 5-MB/s data transfers. (half as fast as a single
fast/wide 7200RPM drive, but a heck of a lot cheaper)

Scott V



