> I have heard of an alpha PC coming out this summer. Could anyne explain
> what this chip is and when it is coming out.

The 21164PC is a low-cost implementation of the Alpha instruction set
(smaller cache -> smaller die size -> cheaper chip), with the addition 
of multimedia instructions (MVI) to speed up graphics and multimedia apps. 
Last I heard, the chip should be shipping in volume this summer.

