Yes, that was a feature of VAXclusters when they were first introduced,
complete with the Star Coupler" (one of the more interesting uses of a
box full of transformers) and the HSC intelligent disk controllers. 
Various forms of hardware sharing have been in 390s for quite a while,
too, but not as generally as they've done it for Sysplex.  I couldn't
say which came first, or if the original VAXcluster was the more general
at introduction.  Nor does it really matter at this point.  S/390 did it
when they decided to give up on bipolar, and get serious about
substituting lots of slower processors for fewer faster ones.  Only this
week, with the latest announcement of the G4 systems, have the CMOS
processors finally gotten faster than the last bipolar processors IBM
shipped (on a uniprocessor basis).

Digital has always been a IBM's major rival in stealth marketing. :-)

