Johan Kellum wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>    I am trying to run a program which needs the command
>    'limit stacksize 32m' on Alpha's, but on a Alpha
>    Station 500 running UNIX version 4.0.C, it does not
>    understand the command.
>    Any help or insight would be greatly appreciated. Thanks!

Hmm .. that works for me (V4.0B).  What shell are you using?
limit is a csh function.  The equivelant function for the bourne
and korn shells is, ulimit. And the syntax is slightly different.

Try 'ulimit -s 32768'.  You want any more than that and you'll
have to bump up max-per-proc-stack-size in the kernel.  Use the
Kernel Tuner GUI admin tool to do that.

