myself.  Problem is most of these are 3 BNC inputs- RGB, often with odd
sync polarity.  I've had good results here using an ATI Mach32 2meg ISA
card that will generate composite sync.  I can't see anything in text
mode, but when X starts, everything is great.  I've also had almost
acceptable results by combining (via ethernet BNC T's), the H&V sync
signals with the green line from one of those 15pinVGA-5BNC video
cables.  Good luck!  If you're interested, a friend of mine build a
hardware device to invert and combine the sync signals automatically. 
