There are two truths - one is that Alpha chips span an extremely broad
range of performance depending on how they are implemented in systems,
the other is that "Pentium level performance" has been completely wildcarded
by the fast clocked Pentiums and Pentium Pros.  System prices also vary
considerably according to the configuration, bus/memory expansion technology
and target market.  Just make sure you're comparing *todays* prices and
claims, anything a few months old admits to too much on confusion, not
to mention letting apples vs. oranges creep into the fray.

