Digital semiconductor, offer's in the moment, two mother-boards for the 
Alpha 21164A processor:

	PC164 366-500MHz w. 1MB Cache, 128/256bits DRAM (4/8xSIMM).
	PC164LX 433-600MHz w. 2MB Cache, 128bits SDRAM (4xDIMM).

Both boards, are equipped with :

	2 x ISA slot's
	2 x PCI-32bit slot's
	2 x PCI-64bit slot's
	1 x PS/2 Mouse interface
	1 x PS/2 Keyboard interface
	2 x RS232 interfase (DB9)
	1 x Centronics interface (DB25)
	Onboard PCI/EIDE controller (CMD)
	Onboard Floppy controller (SMC)
	Onbaord I82378ZB-PCI/ISA Bridge 
	ATX form-factor

In Denmark Digital sell's the processors and MB's for:

	PC164		~$950,-
	PC164LX		~$1100,-

	Alpha 21164A-P5 366Mhz	~$450,-
	Alpha 21164A-P6 433Mhz	~$650,-
	Alpha 21164A-P7 500Mhz	~$950,-
	Alpha 21164A-P8 533Mhz	~$1400,-

I would suspect that prices in the US are somewhat cheaper than
the danish prices listed here.
Also, it should be noticed that the processors mentioned above,
all are NT-Alpha's(not DU). This means that you will not
be able to run Digital-UNIX, but you can still run Linux.
The MB's comes with a CPU fan.

Simular Alpha MB's are also made by Aspen, Microway, Enorex and
many others, and I suspect, without knowing, that they may be a bit
cheaper.

A PC164 MB with a 500MHz Alpha, will in most cases outperform
a dual PPro 200. 

With Digital's FX!32 emulation/translation software, most Intel
apps will run on Alpha/NT(500Mhz), with the same speed as an PPro200.

