too.  See http://www.Nashville.Net/~griffin/video.html for low-cost ($20
- $50) adapters.  They have cables too.
If you have a sync-on-green monitor and your Pee C's graphics card
doesn't support sync-on-green, not to worry... if so inclined you can
build your own adapter (see
http://www.paranoia.com/~filipg/HTML/REPAIR/F_Sync_Green.html) or buy
one from the folks at Griffin mentioned above or Lintec at
http://www.lintec.dk/sync_on_green_adapter.html.  Of course, you have to
program your graphics card for the monitor, and that's where your
Windoze might doze some more.

Be careful when you set up your graphics card!!!  You don't want to let
the smoke out of your monitor!!!

