>The subject Tape Cartridge has gone "end of life" with no recommended
>replacement. Can anyone help me identify the OEM part so I can satisfy my
>customer's requirement? I've heard that it may be the same as a Quantum
>DLT4700 but I want to make sure that an alternative will be software
>compatible.

The Quantum DLT4700 is closer to the TZ887, they the same physical
loader mechanism and use DLT4000/TZ88 drives.  The loader may run
different firmware and the drives certainly have different firmware,
if only to have different Inquiry data.  I suspect there are more
interesting differences lurking deep down inside.

If you want something supported by Digital upgrade to a TZ887.  It
can still read and write CompacTape IIIs and has slightly higher
speed and twice the capacity when using CompacTape IV.  If you
don't need something supported by Digital, go with the DLT4700.

If you need a TZ87/DLT2000 class drive, shop around.
