Niclas Mattsson wrote:
> 
> Just read this from BYTE:
> (see http://www.byte.com/art/9706/sec18/art8.htm)
> 
> "Digital will launch an even more powerful weapon in 1999 to keep the P7
> Merced at bay. The 21364 (EV-7), probably coming out at a similar time
> as Merced, is expected to break the 1-GHz and 100-SPECint95 barriers."
> 
> This is the first I've heard of the 21364. Anyone seen anything else? 

A little bit. According to a DEC executive, EV7 will incorporate
"VLIW-like" technology, among other things. Process technology should be
in the 0.18m range.

Is
> it really due to appear so soon after the 21264? After all, the 21164
> has been around since 1992 ...

21064 was announced in 1992, began shipping late '92
21164 was announced in 1994, began shipping in 1995
21264 was announced in 1996, will ship later this year

There are no technical barriers to the 1999 introduction of a CMOS7
Alpha. Note that a fourth-generation architecture (e.g. 21364) will be
preceded by a CMOS7 shrink of the EV6 architecture. EV67 definitely will
be available in CY99.

Incidentally, good article in Byte. Nebojsa Novakovic is well-informed.



