Mr Man Wai Pang wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>   I need to upgrade an existing 2400 modem to 14.4K on a dec server 200/mc
> for dial in access. I use the same terminal setting as before and just
> replace the modem. When I dail in, the modem can answer and connect but
> cannot access the system, some rubbish comes out. Please help

Sounds like the getty behind the old modem is set for fixed speed
negotiation at 2400 baud. If your new 14k4 has variable rate speed
buffering, then you need to make setting changes to the modem to accept
DTE serial comms from the machine at say 19200 baud (fixed) and allow
the modem to negotiate at any connect speed it can get. You should then
set up your ttys (or which ever file your OS uses) to communicate fixed
rate to your (now fixed rate DTE) modem.

Rob
