WMoisa wrote:
> 
>   I get a message when I start my computer, which is a Telecommander
> Soundwave error.  It saids,"One of the components required for audio is
> not present or is an old version.  Run Setup to re-install the audio
> drivers."  I did, but I still get the same message and afterwards the Task
> window appears.  Will.

There are a number of lines in the SYSTEM.INI that load the different
device drivers. The Wavestream drivers are for the software wavetable
that shipped with the original systems. There are a number of fixes in
the new 32-bit driver release.

Have you loaded the new 32-bit Windows95 drivers for Telecommander? The
new drivers are available at the Digital WEB site at
HTTP://WWW.WINDOWS.DIGITAL.COM. The files are in the DRIVERs section
(Intel library) under the STARION/STARION 9XX-2XXX secrtion. The file
names are:

AD90102B.TXT
AD90102B.EXE

Get both files - the TXT are the instructions - there's also a
readme.txt within the diskette that contains additional information on
loading the new drivers. 

In the readme are specific instructions for delecting selective lines in
the SYSTEM.INI that should fix your problem. You can also use the
instructions to see if your current installation is valid.

regards,

glen kelley



