The decserver 200/MC where MC stood for MODEM CONTROL, i.e. they had the 
carrier detect line identified and you could use remote modems on them, 
unforturnately, their fastest speed was 19200 bps and they ONLY supported LAT. 
I had heard at one time about LAT being ported to Unix but I don't think that 
ever happened. 

The DECserver 700's were as I remember, the first comm server that supported 
TCP/IP as well as LAT. I also think the 700 had uart speed to 57600 or good 
enough to handle 14400 modems. I think you had to go to a 900 to get full 
115200 bps speed out of the unit.

The bottom line is, correct me folks if I am mistaken, you cannot use the 
decserver 200 on anything but a dec vms or dec unix or dec ultrix machine...




