We maybe were late to endorse COSE, however we were pretty quick
in implementing the bigger picture which is the X/Open UNIX 95 standard. 
DIGITAL UNIX was (together with HP-UX on the same day) the first UNIX to get 
the UNIX 95 branding. Most of the current technical work of the major UNIX 
vendor focuses on 64-bit stuff, something we did a long time ago. The next 
step will be OpenGroup's (aka X/Open) UNIX 98 standard. It will include
the 64-bit API model and it is modeled after DIGITAL UNIX (ie. LP64 model).

btw: Solaris still carries no UNIX 95 brand as of June 4, 1997 according
to: http://www.rdg.opengroup.org/public/prods/xu.htm

