One of my first jobs was assisting in the administration of several
VMS machines.  I remember one day coming in to work and finding that
mail had suddenly stopped being delivered.  After spending some time
working my way through the tech support channels at the mail software
provider's tech support, a technician immediately told me what to look
for. 

A log file had reached "maximum" version, which was something like
65535.  The OS refused to update the log file further, completely
constipating the entire mail system.

Call it a fluke, but that episode has caused me to always view
enforced versioning with some suspicion.

joe




