The usual ref for SCCS is

  Rochkind, Marc J.
  Dec. 1975
  The Source Code Control System
  IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering

VMS didn't exist in 1975, so I doubt CMS did.

The standard ref for RCS is

  Design, Implementation, and Evaluation of a Revision Control System
  Tichy, Walter F.
  Proceedings of the 6th International Conference on Software Engineering
  ACM, IEEE, IPS, NBS
  September 1982

I don't remember using CMS until much later in the 80's, and I think
I would have noticed if it were available in 82-83.  (People who came
to VMS later in its life never seem to appreciate how few tools came
with the early versions of VMS!)

Early versions of the MMS docs explicitly acknowledged that it was
modelled on "make".  I don't remember seeing anything similar in the
CMS docs, but I do remember thinking, the first time I saw CMS, that
it was about time VMS provided something equivalent to SCCS.

CMS does predate CVS, which I find to be the best of the bunch.

