CPU bugs...


All the ones I read here are current noise!  Try these:

DEC J-11 FPU math bug.

NEC d8080 early part wasn't fully compatable, actually better but to
users incompatability was a bug.

Early vax designs (11/7xx series) all had soft loaded microcode...
with lots of revisions.

There are a lot of them out there.  For every generation of new cpu
design or implemetation there will be bugs.  The difference in vendors
is how many undiscovered bugs there ther may be. Now with CPUs in the 
millions on transistors testability is (and has) been a major factor.

This is why you will see older CPUs being used for designs where
reliability is paramount.  There bugs are known and can be designed
around.  The best example is the z80/180 chips that were launched in 
1976 and still in production!

