As someone who's business is specifying and buying systems, the only
difference such a rubber stamp makes is in deciding between two equal
systems which both meet the specification in all areas.

How often have you been quoted two equal machines at the same price, one
with UNIX 95 and one without?

The choice is usually simple - pick the cheapest, most powerful system
which runs the software you need to get the job done.  Forget the scout
badges, "Editor's Choice" awards, gold stars, or whatever.  They may be
applicable if you're buying for the US DoD or an organisation of similar
size, but in general they also buy equipment that works rather than
equipment with the right qualifications.

