Huh?  There's so much OpenBoot Prom and SPARC specific crud
in the platform specific part of the kernel, I would be *very*
surprised if you could simply run it through a translator and
get it to boot on an Alpha.  Ranges for mapping interrupt
and clock registers come from the OBP and the layout of those
registers is assumed, not to mention a trap table that also
assumes certain level of registers and, in the case of ultra,
some nifty new register file capabilities.

You've demonstrated this?  You can put unix & genunix through
your translator and get it to work?  Somehow I find this hard
to believe.  Now, userland apps maybe...

