> The article also claims that an AlphaStation 500/500 now has
> the fastest CaffeineMark benchmarks of any UNIX system, and
> has Java numbers that blow out an HP PA-RISC 8200.
> 
> 	-doug
> 
I just downloaded the JIT from Digital and compared it with our
own JIT compiler, the CACAO system which is available at

http://www.complang.tuwien.ac.at/java/cacao/

I just ran three benchmarks, a small loop with an addition, the
sieve benchmark and the java compiler (sun.tools.javac.Main). CACAO
is between 2 and 8 times faster than the JIT from Digital.
The loop is about 3 times faster, the sieve is about 2 times faster
and the javac is about 8 times faster. The funny thing is that for
javac the digital JIT is about 3 times slower than the SUN/OSF
interpreter and that using -nojit for javac is faster than using
-jit. The only problem with CACAO is that the AWT implementation is
not finished, so we have no CaffeineMarks, but the programs of CaffeineMark
which don't use AWT are at least 2 times faster than the Digital JIT.

