In article <5n3vrh$5k2@goliat.c3.hu>, Pecsenyanszky Istvan <pisti@c3.hu> writes:
:We have a VAXserver 3100 with a UQSSP disk controller. We would like to
:add an other one (UQSSP, too). Both of them are working alone as DUA, 
:but not together. How can set (switch) them to work as DUA and DUB?

   There is definitely some confusion here -- the only disk controller
   available for the VAXserver 3100 series is a SCSI controller, and
   the SCSI controller and associated SCSI disk devices do not show up
   as "DUA" devices, rather they show up as "DKA" devices.

   I am guessing this is a Q-bus VAXserver system, not a VAXserver 3100,
   and I am guessing you have some combination of RQDX3, KDA50, or KFQSA
   series UQSSP storage controllers.  (If you don't know the names of the
   controllers, we can likely decode the "M" numbers on the Q-bus module
   spines...)

   You will want to confirm the particular VAXserver system type, and
   you will want to provide information on exactly which UQSSP storage
   controllers are present in the system.  With this, we can help...

  -------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
