Personal Workstations.  After the order was placed, I happened
to be browsing around on the Digital web site, and was dismayed
when I took a close look at the technical specs and discovered
that (according to what's online) these systems don't come with
ethernet.

Now I *suspect* (or at least hope) that the online information
is wrong.  In the first place, I can't believe that in this day
and age, Digital would ship a system without ethernet.  And in
the second place, our sales rep assures me that, yes, they *do*
include ethernet.

Furthermore, I'm not particularly worried in any event, since we
have an e-mail message (two, in fact) from our sales rep, saying
that ethernet is included; so we presumably can insist that they
supply it if the systems arrive without it.  Nonetheless, it does
seem rather weird that an error of that sort could appear (in two
different places) on Digital's own web server.  Check out

 http://www.workstation.digital.com/products/dpwspecs.html

and note the "N/A" which appears as the "Integrated Ethernet"
entry in the au-series column.  Note also that

 http://www.workstation.digital.com/products/auseries/auspec.html

has no entry for "Integrated Ethernet", whereas (for example)

 http://www.workstation.digital.com/products/aseries/aspec.html

does (as does the corresponding page for the i-series).

