In article <01bc6eb6$fd0815c0$d269a5c6@st-mis-aconnock>,
Andy Connock <andy@nlnet.nf.ca> wrote:
>We purchased a TLZ7L-DA backup unit w/ autoloader some time ago...
 
>The DEC docs say the unit is made up of both a TLZ07 backup unit and
>TLZ7L-DA autoloader.  My Seagate docs tell me the SCSI id settings of each
>unit above are supposed to be different.

>The unit/autoloader scsi id settings may not even be a problem.  The SCSI
>card is set to id 7, and the drive is set to id of 3.

On the TLZ7L, the SCSI ID is set by the switches on the back of the
unit.  The drive is at LUN 0 and the autoloader is at LUN 1 of that
SCSI ID.  For your scenario, the drive is ID 3 LUN 0, and the autoloader
is ID 3 LUN 1.

