> Not if your app is single-threaded.

You're assuming that your box is only running one application.  Agreed,
a single threaded app will not gain much benefit by running on a multi-
processor box, but with more processors, you can run *more* processes
before maxing out on CPU.  Or, you can bind your single threaded app
to a CPU, and run multiple instances of it.

I think the Alpha is a pretty cool CPU (I met Dick Sites once),
but Digital's marketing is crap: who the hell wants to buy a great
processor, only to run a crappy OS like NT?

I wasn't overly keen on DU 3.2, but apparently DU4 is a lot better.
AT the end of the day though, I voted with my wallet, and bought
Suns running Solaris (note the Contractor bit in my .sig).

