I still have a MicroVax 2000, and it works just fine running VMS 5.2.  However,
I installed it years ago over the network.  This MV2000 originally had a 42MB
hard disk and a RX33 diskette, now it has an RD53 disk 71MB.  At that time, 
1988 I think, the VMS distribution, V4.6?, was available on diskette, but it
was definitely more than 5 diskettes.  I think diskette distribution was discontinued
with VMS 5.1 as part of DecWindows was included with the operating system.
The small disk, 42MB, configuration was not longer supported either at this point
in time.

What you have is probably "standalone backup".  To use it, you need to have a
backup saveset to restore.  If your saveset, which could be 25 diskettes, is an
image backup, you should have a useable copy VMS, old but useable.  The
procedure would be to boot your standalone backup diskettes, then restore
your image saveset, assuming you can find your saveset diskettes.

By the way, I use my old MV2000 primarily for software testing purposes, not for
development or production.



