In the very few cases I have come across where a single user has sole
access to a system and has a compute-intensive application which
bottlenecks in the processor, and which isn't multi-threaded, the answer
was simple - re-write it to be multi-threaded, and buy a multi-processor
box.

This approach may seem severe, but when the problem needs 3 hours CPU
time on a Cray, and the annual budget for access time is enough to buy a
multi-processor Sun at least 10 times over which can then be thrashed at
25% of the speed for 24 hours a day, the bean counters are in heaven...

