Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I have limited knowledge of this unit, but I would suggest that if you
have only one SCSI ID switch, then it would be probable that it uses two
consecutive SCSI IDs. That being said, the native Windows NT 4mm DAT
driver would only understand a single device and for the Autoloader
functionality you must use a specific driver that understands the unit as
a whole sub-system. As such, it seems to me that you should remove the 4mm
DAT driver and re-install the Seagate software. You should bring up the
Tape Device Control Panel and select other or some such and you will most
likely be prompted to insert the floppy diskette that the Seagate software
is on so that the special driver can be loaded.

This may not seem very intuitive, but it is the mechanism designed by
Microsoft for installing drivers for the Tape Device.

rtt


