On Thu, 29 May 1997 12:34:49 +0100, Marcus Cent <marcus@marcat.co.uk>
wrote:

>I want to convert my C: drive to NTFS on Win NT4. When I try the convert
>utility it tells me that the c:drive is the system partition on an ARC
>compliant system and it cannot be converted. Anyone know what I can do?

The system drive must be FAT, as defined by the ARC specification.

Presumably you want to convert it to NTFS to make it secure. Since you
can't do that, you should instead use Disk Administrator
Partition->Secure System Partition to make the system partition
secure.

You do realise that the system partition only needs to be 6MB?

