> not key-strokes.

That's different. It seems to be saying, "Once a command keystroke has
been pressed -- which ensures that the user's hands are in position to
initiate further actions through the keyboard -- initiation of further
actions through the keyboard must not be allowed."

When I wrote that the cursor movement suite Ctr+P/B/F/N, common in Unix,
is the product of a sick mind, I was joking. If Apple's guidelines say
what you imply they say, I would say they are the product of a sick mind,
and I would be completely serious.

