> arbitrary buttons and fields on arbitrary dialogs.

Taking that literally just to make a point, I wouldn't say I like the
keyboard. (Especially 'cuz I hate redundant keys, which means almost half
the keys on most keyboards today). My hands have to be on the QWERTY keys
most of the time anyway, and people have devised superb, easy-to-learn
ways of doing everything through those keys and Ctrl. Why not use them?

Call me lazy. Using a mouse or non-standard keys is extra work.

